thread:
ben_sales: Kicking off Rivermark POC thread. They want a short pilot: Rust client + streaming SSE, function/tool-calling to enrich transactions, and strict structured JSON output. Primary ask: can we run an air-gapped POC for 2 weeks? Also need a committed-cost estimate for 30 req/s peak, burst to 120qps for 30s.

sophia_se: Air-gapped sounds like Private on-prem. We can do a temporary offline bundle but need network/firewall config and on-site infra checklist. For burst handling we can propose Dedicated with burst lanes or Private with autoscaler config.

omar_dev: Rust SDK supports streaming and tool_calls. Example snippet to register a tool handler and validate structured schema on the client side: 

```rust
let client = redwood::Client::from_env();
let mut stream = client.chat_stream(
  "redwood-infer-2",
  vec![Message::user("Enrich txn { \"id\": 9001 }")],
  StreamOpts::new().enable_tool_calls(vec!["vault.get", "http.fetch"]) .with_structured_schema("{ \"type\": \"object\" }")
).await?;

while let Some(frame) = stream.next().await {
  match frame? {
    StreamFrame::ToolCall(call) => handle_tool(call).await?,
    StreamFrame::Structured(json) => validate_schema(&json)?,
    _ => {}
  }
}
```

omar_dev: Note: tool calls in an air-gapped deployment must be routed to local services. We can't reach external HTTP services unless customer gates egress.

nina_infosec: Security items: SAML SSO, customer-managed KMS, HSM option for keys, IP allowlist, audit log retention 1y+, and pentest/SOC2 artifacts. Air-gapped POC: we need attestation that no telemetry leaves the environment and a signed runbook. Also need to review tool calling surface for privilege escalation vectors.

infra-bot: infra-bot: Created workspace rivermark-poc-2211123456. Temporary creds issued, expire_in: 48h. Provisioned demo cluster in us-east. (Note: air-gapped bundle requires separate ticket).

ben_sales: Good. Pricing: they want an apples-to-apples delta Hosted vs Dedicated vs Private for 2-week POC + 12-month committed option. Can SEs produce a short table? Also legal asked whether customer-managed KMS is supported for Dedicated or only Private.

sophia_se: Quick answers: customer KMS supported on Private; for Dedicated we can offer KMS integration but keys are tenant-scoped in our KMS unless we do a specific commit for CMK export (need legal/ops signoff). I'll include caveats in the quote. I'll draft the cost delta and POC runbook.

omar_dev: For streaming + structured output, call out runtime knobs: batching and kv_cache affect token cost. Recommend batch_target = 4 for low latency, batch_target = 16 for cost efficiency. Also advise max_stream_window_ms for tool calls to avoid long-lived locks.

nina_infosec: I'll start the security questionnaire and request their legal to sign NDA + upload network diagram. For air-gap proof we typically need a joint checklist signed by infra teams.

ben_sales: Plan: Sophia sends cost delta + runbook by Wed EOD; Omar prepares a short Rust demo and a replay script for audit logs; Nina initiates sec questionnaire and NDA; I'll set up Rivermark's contact + schedule a 45m demo next Thu. :calendar:

sophia_se: ACK. Need their preferred data center region and whether they require FIPS endpoints. DM me the contact.

